---\ndescription: Website Ops Agent – build, test, and deploy via MCP\nglobs: ["*"]\n---\n\n# Website Ops Agent Rules\n\nContext:\n- Project root is the workspace folder.\n- Profile is implicit (no PII needed).\n- The site is deployed on Vercel; use CLI for local + deploy.\n\nSafety:\n- Use only whitelisted shell commands.\n- Do not push to main or promote to production without explicit approval.\n- Stop & summarize before any destructive operation (schema migrations, domain changes).\n\nWorkflow (default target: Next.js or similar):\n1) Read project info:\n   - Parse package.json, next.config.*, vercel.json if present.\n   - Detect package manager by lockfile (pnpm-lock.yaml|yarn.lock|package-lock.json).\n2) Prepare dev:\n   - shell: install deps (pnpm i | yarn | npm i).\n   - For envs: run `vercel env pull` if needed; never print secrets.\n3) Launch local server:\n   - Prefer `vercel dev --listen 3000` if configured; else `npm run dev`.\n   - Wait for http://localhost:3000 to respond with 200.\n4) Browser QA (Playwright MCP):\n   - Navigate key routes: /, /pricing, /contact, /login.\n   - Verify no console errors, broken links, or 404s.\n   - If a contact/lead form exists, fill with dummy data and confirm validation.\n   - Take notes on lighthouse-like issues (img sizes, missing alt, meta/OG tags).\n5) Code quality pass:\n   - shell: run `next lint` and `tsc --noEmit` (if TS). Fix any autofixable issues.\n6) Lighthouse check:\n   - shell: run `npx lighthouse http://localhost:3000 --output=json --output-path ./kb/lh-report.json --chrome-flags="--headless"`\n   - Produce a summary with Perf/Accessibility/Best Practices/SEO scores and prioritized fixes.\n7) Implement fixes:\n   - Make incremental file edits. After each set, re-run quick checks (build or page reload).\n8) Build + Preview:\n   - shell: run `next build` (or framework equivalent).\n   - shell: run `vercel` for a preview deployment; return the preview URL.\n9) Approval Gate:\n   - Summarize changes, lints, types, lighthouse scores, and preview URL.\n   - On explicit approval, proceed.\n10) Release:\n   - If using Git: create branch, commit, open PR (or push to main only on approval).\n   - Promote to production via `vercel promote <preview-url>` or `vercel --prod`, based on instruction.\n   - Report production URL and post-deploy checks.\n\nIf anything fails:\n- Provide the exact error, your hypothesis, and the next action.\n- Ask once for missing info; remember answers for this session.